WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.320
The latest episode of The Walking&nbsp;
Dead, "Diverged," picks up shortly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.120
after long-term survivors Carol and Daryl&nbsp;
have had a heartbreaking falling out. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.640
they saunter back toward Alexandria, it's clear&nbsp;
that things between them are still very frosty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.880
and they come to a literal fork in the road.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.360
In the fifth episode of The Walking Dead's&nbsp;
season 10C, Carol's search for a problem to solve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.000
begins with her picking up a tattered&nbsp;
scarf off the streets of Alexandria.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.240
When she finds Jerry working in one of&nbsp;
the fields, he eyes the dirty fabric;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.760
Carol explains that she wants&nbsp;
to wash it and mend the holes.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.240
"Somebody loved it and I&nbsp;
just want to fix something."

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.760
Although Jerry seems a little concerned, he also&nbsp;
doesn't have any other task for Carol to take on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.160
She creates one for herself by announcing that&nbsp;
she'll contribute to the rebuilding efforts by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.760
making a pot of soup for everyone. However, that&nbsp;
seemingly simple assignment doesn't go as planned.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.360
Some of the problems Carol encounters&nbsp;
while making the soup stem from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.280
hardships of post-apocalyptic life.&nbsp;
However, others are the result of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.600
her anxious desire to fix things pulling&nbsp;
her attention in different directions.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.880
She starts and stops the project many times,&nbsp;
taking detours to collect more greens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.240
make an improvised rat trap to try and catch a&nbsp;
rodent that's invaded her home, and fix a solar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.040
panel so that she can get her trusty crock&nbsp;
pot working again. By the time night falls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:26.400
none of the issues have been resolved: the rat is&nbsp;
still loose, the soup is still just ingredients,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.040
and the scarf is still a tattered rag.&nbsp;
In her harried desire to fix something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:36.080
Carol ends up not accomplishing anything&nbsp;
other than driving herself into a dark mood.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.040
While Carol struggles with her soup,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.720
Daryl is having a difficult time&nbsp;
completing his own scavenging mission.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.320
His quest to repair the motorbike&nbsp;
takes the better part of the day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.000
and sees him having several close&nbsp;
calls with walkers. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.080
he's able to get the bike working again&nbsp;
and even finds some useful supplies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.800
but it's clear that his falling out with Carol&nbsp;
both figuratively and literally set him back.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.240
The irony of "Diverged" is that Carol and Daryl&nbsp;
spend the episode apart looking for a solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:09.200
to a problem that the other could easily&nbsp;
solve. If Daryl hadn't pushed Carol away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:14.160
he'd have the tool he needs to fix his bike, and&nbsp;
if Carol hadn't left, she'd have something she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.520
could easily fix. Had they not started the episode&nbsp;
by going down diverging paths in the woods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.240
everything would have been much simpler for both&nbsp;
of them. However, as anyone who has ever had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:29.360
falling out with a good friend knows, sometimes&nbsp;
there's no easy fix for a problem like this.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:35.200
While Daryl remains stoic, Carol gives viewers&nbsp;
some more direct insight into how she's feeling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.760
confiding in Dog while the&nbsp;
two are cuddling in bed.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.080
"He'll&nbsp;
come back. He always comes back."

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.040
Although she expresses hope for Daryl's return,&nbsp;
she is much more pessimistic in her assessment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.440
of herself, wondering if everyone would be&nbsp;
better off if she just got out of their hair.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:57.760
During the night, Dog wakes Carol up because&nbsp;
he can hear the rat scurrying around somewhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:04.160
behind the walls. Unable to let the problem go&nbsp;
unsolved, Carol furiously rips apart the drywall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.000
leaving behind a massive physical&nbsp;
manifestation of her woes.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Jerry picks up on this the next day&nbsp;
when he stops by to pay Carol a visit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.040
Although the soup is finally&nbsp;
bubbling away in the crockpot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.120
she's clearly still carrying around a&nbsp;
lot of pain. Jerry offers to tell her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.360
one of Ezekiel's sayings to give her some&nbsp;
perspective. But Carol isn't interested.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.200
"Maybe I don't need&nbsp;
a saying. Maybe I just need to fix what I broke."

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.000
In "Find Me," Daryl blamed Carol for the&nbsp;
disappearance of his close friend Connie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.040
who was lost in a cave&nbsp;
collapse that, as he sees it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.400
was caused by Carol recklessly seeking&nbsp;
revenge on Whisperer leader Alpha.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:45.200
Although Carol believes that her actions were in&nbsp;
service of a greater good, she still understands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.200
that they came with negative consequences&nbsp;
and the guilt of it weighs heavily on her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:53.520
It's not the first time we've seen her struggle&nbsp;
in this regard, but Daryl being the one to pin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.240
the blame on her seems to be a twist of the&nbsp;
knife that may be too much for her to bear.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:01.440
Jerry has already intuited that her&nbsp;
pain has something to do with Daryl.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.040
"A friend is someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:06.320
who thinks you're perfect even if&nbsp;
everyone else thinks you're broken."

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.600
Carol isn't buying it, though.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.360
"What if you really are broken?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.280
What if your best friend just realized it&nbsp;
a whole lot later than everyone else did?"

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:21.360
After her conversation with Jerry, Carol&nbsp;
apologizes to the tattered scarf before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.880
abandoning her plans to repair it&nbsp;
and throwing it in the garbage.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.640
She walks outside and sees Daryl&nbsp;
getting home from his scavenging trip.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.760
The two have a stilted conversation and, when&nbsp;
Carol tries to give the Swiss Army knife back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.720
Daryl tells her to keep it. The episode ends&nbsp;
with them each going into their separate homes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:41.360
no closer to reaching any kind of solution.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.840
It's clear that this rough&nbsp;
patch in their relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:48.880
is painful for both Carol and Daryl, but that&nbsp;
neither is quite sure how to navigate it.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:53.280
The characters have known each other for a&nbsp;
long time and have been through a lot together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:57.120
but long-term relationships of any kind are&nbsp;
difficult; they have their ups and downs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.760
and sometimes they unfortunately break apart.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.680
It's possible that this low-point for&nbsp;
Carol and Daryl will pass and we'll see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.920
them buddied up again — presumably just in&nbsp;
time for the Daryl-Carol spin-off series.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.360
For now, though, it looks like their&nbsp;
sorrow for the people they've lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.360
and the guilt of their decisions are going to&nbsp;
keep them at arm's length from one another.

